    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0564" n="492" xml:id="pg492"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Judd to Mrs.
                            Lincoln</hi>.</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1865-05-01">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 1, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Honored Madam</hi>: I have the honor to inform you
                    that to-day Captain Von Lucadon, personal aide-de-camp of his Royal Highness the
                    Crown Prince of Prussia, called at this legation, by command of his Royal
                    Highness, charged to convey to you, madam, through me, the sympathy that their
                    royal highnesses, the Prince and the Princess Royal feel for your deep
                    affliction, in the death of your worthy and honored husband, and their anxious
                    desire for your health and well-being.</p>
                <p>In executing that request, permit me to add, on my own behalf, the sincere
                    sympathy I feel for your loss, and the deep grief that overwhelmed me at the
                    death of one to whom I was bound by the strongest ties of friendship and
                    love.</p>
                <p>I am, madam, your obedient servant and friend,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>N. B. JUDD,</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">United States Minister, Prussia</hi>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Abraham Lincoln</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
